            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a knife, then the Urdu for a fork; a thorn."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بوتل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بوتل — botal — \"a bottle\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بوتل (botal) is usually traced to English bottle; some trace it to Portuguese botelha, \"bottle\", which reached India first. CDIAL has no entry for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
